{
 "result": "maze.py is a flat-grid BFS. It pads the input with a '#' border into one bytes buffer, uses a bytearray as the visited map, and expands frontier lists level by level, returning as soon as E is reached (or -1 when the queue empties). It passes all three public samples (2008, -1, 78). The assay registered a baseline of 3.477 (noise 6.2%). I did not try further speedups, such as bidirectional BFS, because a win must beat the baseline by more than 6.2% and the current body is already simple and correct.",
